(5210310, 756770, 102426, '<td valign="top">i do not understand how this is ansel adam''s style.</td>', 'i do not understand how this is ansel adam''s style.', '2009-01-21 18:51:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210312, 757699, 102426, '<td valign="top">interesting, it makes me want to know more.</td>', 'interesting, it makes me want to know more.', '2009-01-21 18:51:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210326, 758136, 86447, '<td valign="top">LOL @ your title... it does look nice and straight...  :)</td>', 'LOL @ your title... it does look nice and straight...  :)', '2009-01-21 18:55:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210334, 757143, 86447, '<td valign="top">Ummm... awful border, but semi-interesting image.  Good contrast.</td>', 'Ummm... awful border, but semi-interesting image.  Good contrast.', '2009-01-21 19:01:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210360, 757968, 101822, '<td valign="top">Beautiful, but I think it''s too sharp - and in my opinion would look more dramatic from a lower angleand the house thing slightly more to the left of the frame.</td>', 'Beautiful, but I think it''s too sharp - and in my opinion would look more dramatic from a lower angleand the house thing slightly more to the left of the frame.', '2009-01-21 19:27:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210363, 757044, 101822, '<td valign="top">Wowee. The sky is dramatically beautiful - the only improvement in this photo might be to have framed a bit more to the right</td>', 'Wowee. The sky is dramatically beautiful - the only improvement in this photo might be to have framed a bit more to the right', '2009-01-21 19:28:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210364, 758351, 102513, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot!</td>', 'Very nice shot!', '2009-01-21 19:29:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210371, 757556, 101822, '<td valign="top">It''s not the prettiest picture but - I love the idea !</td>', 'It''s not the prettiest picture but - I love the idea !', '2009-01-21 19:31:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210376, 758016, 101822, '<td valign="top">Wow, this scene is stunning-  I think the trees in the top left are distracting, though</td>', 'Wow, this scene is stunning-  I think the trees in the top left are distracting, though', '2009-01-21 19:33:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210379, 757315, 101822, '<td valign="top">Oh <br/>wow.<br/>Breathtaking view</td>', 'Oh wow.Breathtaking view', '2009-01-21 19:35:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210386, 757096, 101822, '<td valign="top">It''s a shame those foreground trees are distracting ..<br/>Nonetheless, this composition is great.</td>', 'It''s a shame those foreground trees are distracting ..Nonetheless, this composition is great.', '2009-01-21 19:36:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210407, 758069, 101822, '<td valign="top">I love the light over the little tree - but this shot seems a bit busy</td>', 'I love the light over the little tree - but this shot seems a bit busy', '2009-01-21 19:39:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210502, 758263, 101445, '<td valign="top">This is my favorite of the challenge - great sky in back and white and the rocks are great</td>', 'This is my favorite of the challenge - great sky in back and white and the rocks are great', '2009-01-21 20:18:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210515, 758218, 101492, '<td valign="top">Her backside becomes the focal point instead of the view, not very Ansel Adams-like</td>', 'Her backside becomes the focal point instead of the view, not very Ansel Adams-like', '2009-01-21 20:28:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210525, 757145, 101492, '<td valign="top">I like the composition, but the contrast seems too harsh.</td>', 'I like the composition, but the contrast seems too harsh.', '2009-01-21 20:34:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210546, 758280, 101492, '<td valign="top">Focus?</td>', 'Focus?', '2009-01-21 20:41:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210553, 756931, 101492, '<td valign="top">Great sky.</td>', 'Great sky.', '2009-01-21 20:45:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210579, 756797, 54645, '<td valign="top">One of the few that maintains high contrast along with detail. I suspect that this is even better at a larger size. It seems surreal, in that the building feels small, like a model, so possibly utilizing more foreground to give the building scale, particularly in an Ansel Adams challenge.</td>', 'One of the few that maintains high contrast along with detail. I suspect that this is even better at a larger size. It seems surreal, in that the building feels small, like a model, so possibly utilizing more foreground to give the building scale, particularly in an Ansel Adams challenge.', '2009-01-21 20:56:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210617, 758232, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is one of the better renderings of snow/ice in the challenge, and that''s one of the most difficult things to do well in post processing. The more so when you have deep shadows to contend with. Nice job!</td>', 'This is one of the better renderings of snow/ice in the challenge, and that''s one of the most difficult things to do well in post processing. The more so when you have deep shadows to contend with. Nice job!', '2009-01-21 21:19:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210625, 758347, 30861, '<td valign="top">This one is beautifully rendered, with the deep foreground shadows fully detailed and expressed. For my tastes it''s a little oversharpened, and the sky''s a little too dark &amp; even. I realize you had to take what you were given with the sky, but keeping it overall half a zone lighter then throwing a gradient in from the top would have given a little depth to the sky and made the imkage a bit more powerful, I think. Still, very nice work.</td>', 'This one is beautifully rendered, with the deep foreground shadows fully detailed and expressed. For my tastes it''s a little oversharpened, and the sky''s a little too dark & even. I realize you had to take what you were given with the sky, but keeping it overall half a zone lighter then throwing a gradient in from the top would have given a little depth to the sky and made the imkage a bit more powerful, I think. Still, very nice work.', '2009-01-21 21:23:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210640, 757676, 30861, '<td valign="top">There''s a LOT to like in this image, but it hasn''t reached its fullest potential. I have basically two issues:<br/> <br/>1. Overall the landscape tones are muddy, local area contrast is needed. Not a lot more, but some. If you look at it analytically, you''ll realize that there''s nearly as much contrast on the back of the arch as there is on the landscape itself, and that''s just unnatural.<br/> <br/>2. There''s a basic sense of the two primary backlit portions of the image (the foreground and the arch) being "outlined" by lighter tonalities: see how the lightest portion of the near landscape is following the outline of the foreground rocks? And ditto the sky above the arch. It leaves the impression that you were dodging the arch and the rocks, and the dodging overlapped into the landscape and the sky. Even if this isn''t the case, that''s what it looks like, and it''s a flaw, although not a seriously disturbing one. That is to say, the haloing is diffuse enough to not be totally distracting.<br/> <br/>Withal, a strong entry and one of my good-scoring choices.</td>', 'There''s a LOT to like in this image, but it hasn''t reached its fullest potential. I have basically two issues: 1. Overall the landscape tones are muddy, local area contrast is needed. Not a lot more, but some. If you look at it analytically, you''ll realize that there''s nearly as much contrast on the back of the arch as there is on the landscape itself, and that''s just unnatural. 2. There''s a basic sense of the two primary backlit portions of the image (the foreground and the arch) being "outlined" by lighter tonalities: see how the lightest portion of the near landscape is following the outline of the foreground rocks? And ditto the sky above the arch. It leaves the impression that you were dodging the arch and the rocks, and the dodging overlapped into the landscape and the sky. Even if this isn''t the case, that''s what it looks like, and it''s a flaw, although not a seriously disturbing one. That is to say, the haloing is diffuse enough to not be totally distracting. Withal, a strong entry and one of my good-scoring choices.', '2009-01-21 21:30:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210646, 757485, 66041, '<td valign="top">Very nice indeed</td>', 'Very nice indeed', '2009-01-21 21:33:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210650, 757938, 30861, '<td valign="top">It is unfortunate that the truncated, central tree is aligned with the aspen trunk behind it; moving the POV slightly to left or right would have avoided this and better expressed the depth in the scene. The snow''s a little blown out in the center, also, so it competes with the very luminous aspen leaves. The filigree of twigs that define the foreground is unexpected and pleasing. A strong entry IMO, but one that could have been even stronger.</td>', 'It is unfortunate that the truncated, central tree is aligned with the aspen trunk behind it; moving the POV slightly to left or right would have avoided this and better expressed the depth in the scene. The snow''s a little blown out in the center, also, so it competes with the very luminous aspen leaves. The filigree of twigs that define the foreground is unexpected and pleasing. A strong entry IMO, but one that could have been even stronger.', '2009-01-21 21:33:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210652, 758099, 66041, '<td valign="top">Very nice.   I might have trimmed some of the sky out to make more of a panorama-feel to the image, given your subject (trees) leaves me with that feeling to begin with</td>', 'Very nice.   I might have trimmed some of the sky out to make more of a panorama-feel to the image, given your subject (trees) leaves me with that feeling to begin with', '2009-01-21 21:34:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210657, 758329, 30861, '<td valign="top">Very, very nice job on the luminosity of the ice; a difficult thing to do well. I don''t feel that the foreground is doing the image justice. I find that by cropping off half the water I can make the composition MUCH stronger. Try it and see what you think.</td>', 'Very, very nice job on the luminosity of the ice; a difficult thing to do well. I don''t feel that the foreground is doing the image justice. I find that by cropping off half the water I can make the composition MUCH stronger. Try it and see what you think.', '2009-01-21 21:36:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210659, 758278, 66041, '<td valign="top">I love the composition, but the picture doesn''t pop.  Feels like it needs a B&amp;W filter or such applied to it to turn a good composition into a great photograph.</td>', 'I love the composition, but the picture doesn''t pop.  Feels like it needs a B&W filter or such applied to it to turn a good composition into a great photograph.', '2009-01-21 21:36:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210670, 757851, 30861, '<td valign="top">Nicely rendered in all respects except that the sky is not working for you at all. A quick mask of the sky area followed by a black-to-transparent gradient laid over the sky on a multiply layer would have done wonders to increase the visual depth of the image and take it to the next level.<br/> <br/>I took the liberty of doing this very quickly; the mask was not refined, so there''s a little bit of edge haloing, but this can easily be avoided working carefully at higher resolution. What do you think of the change?<br/> <br/>//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=758541</td>', 'Nicely rendered in all respects except that the sky is not working for you at all. A quick mask of the sky area followed by a black-to-transparent gradient laid over the sky on a multiply layer would have done wonders to increase the visual depth of the image and take it to the next level. I took the liberty of doing this very quickly; the mask was not refined, so there''s a little bit of edge haloing, but this can easily be avoided working carefully at higher resolution. What do you think of the change? //www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=758541', '2009-01-21 21:43:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210674, 758135, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is a sweet image, but IMO it hasn''t been processed to its full potential. There''s a little more luminosity to be had, a little better expression of the deep shadows, if you reach for it. Very nicely seen, however :-)</td>', 'This is a sweet image, but IMO it hasn''t been processed to its full potential. There''s a little more luminosity to be had, a little better expression of the deep shadows, if you reach for it. Very nicely seen, however :-)', '2009-01-21 21:45:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210679, 757346, 98022, '<td valign="top">Nice composition and tones, but seems a little soft.</td>', 'Nice composition and tones, but seems a little soft.', '2009-01-21 21:48:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210681, 757455, 98022, '<td valign="top">Great foreground interest. Nice composition.</td>', 'Great foreground interest. Nice composition.', '2009-01-21 21:49:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210684, 758190, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is a lovely image, very inviting. I love the keyline on this one, too. However, the softness of the sky is very offputting to me in the context of the rest of the image, and especially in the context of an AA challenge, because he worked hard to make his clouds crisp. Even the landscape itself is softening in the BG, you have a surprisingly limited DOF. Ansel, on the other hand, was known for the deep clarity of his images, he used very small apertures and the tilts on his view camera to attain maximum usable DOF.<br/> <br/>The rendering of the tones, on the other hand, is absolutely first rate, and overall it''s a very, very pleasing image. It''s just that, for THIS challenge, I''d prefer to see it crisper in the depths and in the sky.</td>', 'This is a lovely image, very inviting. I love the keyline on this one, too. However, the softness of the sky is very offputting to me in the context of the rest of the image, and especially in the context of an AA challenge, because he worked hard to make his clouds crisp. Even the landscape itself is softening in the BG, you have a surprisingly limited DOF. Ansel, on the other hand, was known for the deep clarity of his images, he used very small apertures and the tilts on his view camera to attain maximum usable DOF. The rendering of the tones, on the other hand, is absolutely first rate, and overall it''s a very, very pleasing image. It''s just that, for THIS challenge, I''d prefer to see it crisper in the depths and in the sky.', '2009-01-21 21:50:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210693, 758037, 30861, '<td valign="top">The scene is quintessentially Adams, from his introspective moods, but the rendering falls short of what it might be. See //z.about.com/d/govegas/1/0/P/X/aspensdawnbeladams.jpg for a similar scene by AA, and how he handled the tonalities. You have much of that potential here.</td>', 'The scene is quintessentially Adams, from his introspective moods, but the rendering falls short of what it might be. See //z.about.com/d/govegas/1/0/P/X/aspensdawnbeladams.jpg for a similar scene by AA, and how he handled the tonalities. You have much of that potential here.', '2009-01-21 21:55:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210701, 757453, 30861, '<td valign="top">Well, this is a classic Ansel scene, of course; you''re standing in the man''s footsteps :-) The light is less expressive than it might be, very flat along the left of the image, and this is hurting you, though of course I recognize you wouldn''t have had the luxury of camping out there for days on end waiting for the perfect light and clouds. The rendering of tones is quite good, except the thickest clouds seem rather blown out. For me it''s a little oversharpened, but this is SO dependent on differences in monitors that I disregard it. Nice homage to the master.</td>', 'Well, this is a classic Ansel scene, of course; you''re standing in the man''s footsteps :-) The light is less expressive than it might be, very flat along the left of the image, and this is hurting you, though of course I recognize you wouldn''t have had the luxury of camping out there for days on end waiting for the perfect light and clouds. The rendering of tones is quite good, except the thickest clouds seem rather blown out. For me it''s a little oversharpened, but this is SO dependent on differences in monitors that I disregard it. Nice homage to the master.', '2009-01-21 21:58:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210705, 757822, 30861, '<td valign="top">Beautifully expressive light, great development of tones, but way too crowded in the frame (I''m sure you were backed up against something, LOL) and just too extreme in its convergence for my tastes. Still, nice grasp of Zone System principles as far as processing goes.</td>', 'Beautifully expressive light, great development of tones, but way too crowded in the frame (I''m sure you were backed up against something, LOL) and just too extreme in its convergence for my tastes. Still, nice grasp of Zone System principles as far as processing goes.', '2009-01-21 22:01:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210709, 757145, 86340, '<td valign="top">it''s too dark and also overblown. There''s not much in between</td>', 'it''s too dark and also overblown. There''s not much in between', '2009-01-21 22:03:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210710, 757773, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is very sweet. It''s a little too chaotic in the foreground for my tastes, but that''s personal :-) Nicely rendered, nice subtle variation in the sky out towards the edges. In fact, in general you understand the virtues of darkening all four edges of the image oh-so-slightly.</td>', 'This is very sweet. It''s a little too chaotic in the foreground for my tastes, but that''s personal :-) Nicely rendered, nice subtle variation in the sky out towards the edges. In fact, in general you understand the virtues of darkening all four edges of the image oh-so-slightly.', '2009-01-21 22:03:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210715, 757677, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is a lovely image. It''s nicely rendered, the tonalities are fully expressed. I''ve never seen an "aerial" Adams, but that''s neither here nor there as far as I''m concerned; you''ve got the tonal range nailed, and it''s compositionally intriguing, and those are what count.</td>', 'This is a lovely image. It''s nicely rendered, the tonalities are fully expressed. I''ve never seen an "aerial" Adams, but that''s neither here nor there as far as I''m concerned; you''ve got the tonal range nailed, and it''s compositionally intriguing, and those are what count.', '2009-01-21 22:05:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5210719, 756833, 86340, '<td valign="top">on my monitor (which is calibrated) i''m picking up some light brownish/red. Great dof and light on the cactus</td>', 'on my monitor (which is calibrated) i''m picking up some light brownish/red. Great dof and light on the cactus', '2009-01-21 22:08:04.000000', NULL, 1),
