(5225344, 757556, 88136, '<td valign="top">lol well i thought it was a cool idea. dont be too discouraged, i did reeelly freaking bad in my first challenge too. we all get better</td>', 'lol well i thought it was a cool idea. dont be too discouraged, i did reeelly freaking bad in my first challenge too. we all get better', '2009-01-28 22:34:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5225378, 756849, 5475, '<td valign="top">This has the composition of an Ansel Adam''s shot, but not the editing.  He makes the sky nearly black, and would have much more contrast in the mountains.  I think you have the winning shot here, but only if you had edited it more in Ansel''s style.  Beautiful shot!  Take care,<br/>JD</td>', 'This has the composition of an Ansel Adam''s shot, but not the editing.  He makes the sky nearly black, and would have much more contrast in the mountains.  I think you have the winning shot here, but only if you had edited it more in Ansel''s style.  Beautiful shot!  Take care,JD', '2009-01-28 22:53:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5225495, 756849, 65319, '<td valign="top">Breathtaking...I gave this stunning image a 9.  Congrats on your HM!</td>', 'Breathtaking...I gave this stunning image a 9.  Congrats on your HM!', '2009-01-29 01:04:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5225575, 757211, 60195, '<td valign="top">You just keep getting better and better, Joe.  When does your book come out?  No, seriously.<br/>As much as this version says "Ansel" to me, I think I actually like the color version better.  <br/>Awesome post, as usual. Congrats on the Blue :O)</td>', 'You just keep getting better and better, Joe.  When does your book come out?  No, seriously.As much as this version says "Ansel" to me, I think I actually like the color version better.  Awesome post, as usual. Congrats on the Blue :O)', '2009-01-29 02:53:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5225753, 757031, 81362, '<td valign="top">This really captures a sense of the sparkling play of light in a place expected to be dark. Dynamic range handled well, and just enugh deviation from symmetry for sustained interest.</td>', 'This really captures a sense of the sparkling play of light in a place expected to be dark. Dynamic range handled well, and just enugh deviation from symmetry for sustained interest.', '2009-01-29 08:36:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5225785, 757556, 81362, '<td valign="top">Welcome to the challenges. For the voting and scores, it helps to remember your purpose in submitting - to learn, instead of to gather scores. Sometimes comments help with that, sometimes not. But you can always learn from having attempted to meet a challenge and then noticing in detail how others approached the topic. Still, you were not last place.<br/> <br/>As you have discovered, along with many of us, studio set up shots are not easy. Your subject is complex. Moving the background further away would eliminate some of the distrating variation. Not sure why the spoon appears out of focus, but that does diminish the visual appeal. Consider reading up on all the different factors that affect depth of field besides the f stop.</td>', 'Welcome to the challenges. For the voting and scores, it helps to remember your purpose in submitting - to learn, instead of to gather scores. Sometimes comments help with that, sometimes not. But you can always learn from having attempted to meet a challenge and then noticing in detail how others approached the topic. Still, you were not last place. As you have discovered, along with many of us, studio set up shots are not easy. Your subject is complex. Moving the background further away would eliminate some of the distrating variation. Not sure why the spoon appears out of focus, but that does diminish the visual appeal. Consider reading up on all the different factors that affect depth of field besides the f stop.', '2009-01-29 09:15:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5225817, 757211, 52115, '<td valign="top">I always think of Jack Daniels, whose famous from In Kentucky here. A shot well done in the Ansel Adams style.</td>', 'I always think of Jack Daniels, whose famous from In Kentucky here. A shot well done in the Ansel Adams style.', '2009-01-29 09:54:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5225937, 758016, 714, '<td valign="top">This is so pretty!  should of taken first IMHO.</td>', 'This is so pretty!  should of taken first IMHO.', '2009-01-29 11:12:58.000000', NULL, 0),
